<!--
    IL2CPP STRIPPING GUARD.

    The Android build compiles with `managedStrippingLevel: High`
    (ProjectSettings). High stripping treats members that are ONLY ever
    called through reflection as unused and deletes them - and content
    loading is entirely reflection:

        ContentLoader.cs -> JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<T>(text, Settings)

    The scope is kept narrow: only the two assemblies that are read
    reflectively. `preserve="all"` keeps every type and member; these
    assemblies are small (POCOs + Newtonsoft), so the size cost is
    negligible.

    ===================================================================
    THIS GUARD WAS MEASURED ON 14 SEPTEMBER - BEFORE THAT IT HAD NEVER
    BEEN RUN.

    The earlier version of this comment said "nothing shows up in the
    editor or in a Windows build, so this bug lives in the one
    configuration NO test in the project can reach". That was true, and
    it is exactly what made it a problem: the guard had been written by
    reasoning and never EXECUTED. A check that does not run looks exactly
    like one that passes.

    It runs now. See docs/46, and no device is needed:

        .\tools\unity\tour.ps1 -Build windows-il2cpp

    That builds Windows with Android's compiler and stripper (IL2CPP +
    High) and runs the tour's checks against it. With this file in place
    129 checks pass; REMOVE IT and the game dies on startup.

    THE MEASUREMENT CORRECTED THE COMMENT. The symptom expected was "a
    silent default: every field comes back zero or null". The real
    symptom is harsher and earlier:

        could not load the content: JsonSerializationException: Unable to
        find a constructor to use for type Lokanta.Content.EconomyDto

    What gets stripped is not the property SETTERS but the DTOs'
    CONSTRUCTORS - Newtonsoft cannot build the object at all.
    ContentSetLoader cannot load, the game carries on in a half state and
    dies eight checks later with a NullReferenceException; it never even
    reaches the error screen.

    So the danger was described correctly and the mechanism was wrong.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="Lokanta.Content" preserve="all" />
  <assembly fullname="Newtonsoft.Json" preserve="all" />
</linker>
